  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nVectorized, numerically stable reference implementation following exact specifications.\n\n### 💻 Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef value_iteration_step(values: list, transitions: list, rewards: list, gamma: float) -> list[float]:\n    v_arr = np.array(values, dtype=float)\n    T = np.array(transitions, dtype=float)\n    R = np.array(rewards, dtype=float)\n    n_states, n_actions = R.shape\n    new_v = []\n    for s in range(n_states):\n        q_vals = []\n        for a in range(n_actions):\n            q = R[s, a] + gamma * np.sum(T[s, a] * v_arr)\n            q_vals.append(q)\n        new_v.append(round(float(max(q_vals)), 6))\n    return new_v\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for memory buffers.\n",
